1
00:00:00,709 --> 00:00:02,836
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:14,681
<i>They had us slaughtered</i>
<i>like we were animals.</i>

3
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:16,266
<i>Is that why you came back here?</i>

4
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:17,934
<i>To get back at my family?</i>

5
00:00:18,018 --> 00:00:19,936
<i>Ivy, seeking revenge won't solve anything.</i>

6
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:21,604
<i>It'll only be harder on you.</i>

7
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:26,651
<i>If you don't tell me</i>
<i>where Miss Ivy Aguas is,</i>

8
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:28,361
<i>you'll see what I'm capable of.</i>

9
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:31,114
<i>I need to find out who filed</i>
<i>the police report against Raul.</i>

10
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:32,824
[Belen] <i>He kidnapped Jasmin.</i>

11
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:35,285
<i>Do you know what Jasmin's full name is?</i>

12
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:39,247
<i>A woman I spoke to called her Camia.</i>

13
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:40,832
[Raul] <i>Camia's gone, she dead!</i>

14
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:42,250
<i>Isn't that what you want to hear?</i>

15
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:43,793
<i>Why are you so obsessed with her?</i>

16
00:00:43,877 --> 00:00:45,545
<i>Because I love Camia.</i>

17
00:00:45,628 --> 00:00:48,006
<i>I need to bury her back</i>
<i>in the grave she crawled out of!</i>

18
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,966
<i>If it weren't for your womanizing,</i>

19
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:53,178
<i>none of this would've happened</i>
<i>to Lily or our family!</i>

20
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:55,930
<i>What family? You aren't related</i>
<i>to the Ardientes.</i>

21
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:57,849
<i>Emilia's not your real mother.</i>

22
00:00:57,932 --> 00:01:00,268
<i>Camia Cruz, a woman Mom killed</i>
<i>a long time ago.</i>

23
00:01:00,351 --> 00:01:01,269
<i>She's still alive.</i>

24
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:05,523
<i>Killing is the only thing you know,</i>
<i>and yet, you still fail.</i>

25
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:06,983
<i>I will fix this problem, Papa.</i>

26
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:09,360
<i>I will fix this problem myself.</i>

27
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:11,613
<i>You can't look for her.</i>

28
00:01:11,696 --> 00:01:13,073
<i>First of all, you have no machinery.</i>

29
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:17,327
<i>Let me make my own machinery.</i>
<i>Take me to Ivy Aguas.</i>

30
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:21,247
<i>I need to be ready in case</i>
<i>Emilia figures us out.</i>

31
00:01:21,331 --> 00:01:23,249
<i>Books and other stuff.</i>

32
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:28,171
<i>They might help jog your memories, Mom.</i>

33
00:01:28,254 --> 00:01:33,301
<i>Dante… Lily, my daughter…</i>
<i>My daughter… Lily…</i>

34
00:01:36,805 --> 00:01:39,808
[tense music playing]

35
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:56,658
Was that Arnaldo's car
I heard leaving just then?

36
00:01:56,741 --> 00:01:57,867
Yes, Congressman.

37
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:03,456
How curious…

38
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:10,839
He didn't tell me he was going.

39
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:20,765
[panting]

40
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:23,852
Mom, do you remember Dad?

41
00:02:26,896 --> 00:02:28,606
Yes. Yes.

42
00:02:29,023 --> 00:02:32,152
I remember Dante. He made this.

43
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:38,950
How about Lily?

44
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:42,662
-Yes. Yes.
-Really?

45
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:47,500
I remember Lily.
She's the one in this photo.

46
00:02:48,877 --> 00:02:50,879
Where is she? I want to see her.

47
00:02:54,507 --> 00:02:55,842
-She's here.
-Let me see her.

48
00:02:57,010 --> 00:02:58,261
You're looking at her, Mom.

49
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:01,347
It's been 13 years already.

50
00:03:02,932 --> 00:03:07,979
I'm not a kid anymore.
I'm all grown up. See? I'm Lily.

51
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:10,982
No. No.

52
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:19,616
Thirteen years?
It hasn't been that long yet.

53
00:03:21,534 --> 00:03:23,286
You aren't Lily.

54
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:25,371
Why can't I remember anything?

55
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:27,373
Why can't I remember who you are?

56
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:30,251
Why are we here? What are we doing here?

57
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:33,963
Why are we hiding? Who are we hiding from?

58
00:03:35,506 --> 00:03:40,470
I'm so confused! Tell me! Why are we here?

59
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:47,018
I'm sorry for causing you so much trouble.

60
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:49,687
No, you're not. It's okay, Mom.

61
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:52,857
Don't blame yourself for what happened.

62
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:55,693
I'm here to take care of you…

63
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:58,071
and help you regain your memories.

64
00:03:58,154 --> 00:04:01,950
Please don't force yourself
to remember anything.

65
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:04,911
It's not your fault, Mom. Take it easy.

66
00:04:25,014 --> 00:04:27,725
Hi. Good morning. Is Miss Aguas here?

67
00:04:27,809 --> 00:04:28,768
Ma'am, I'm sorry,

68
00:04:28,851 --> 00:04:31,437
but we aren't allowed to accept
any visitors at the moment.

69
00:04:31,896 --> 00:04:34,148
Look, we aren't your typical guests.

70
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:37,235
This is a courtesy call from the mayor.

71
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:40,655
And the former governor
of Poblacion Ardiente.

72
00:04:43,574 --> 00:04:47,287
Didn't I tell you
I won't entertain any guests?

73
00:04:47,578 --> 00:04:50,290
Ma'am, I'm sorry. They're
just really persistent.

74
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:52,083
Courtesy call from the mayor.

75
00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:54,711
<i>I'll just ask them to leave, ma'am.</i>

76
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:58,298
No, now you can't do that!
They'll suspect something.

77
00:04:58,673 --> 00:05:00,174
I'm really sorry, ma'am.

78
00:05:00,591 --> 00:05:03,136
Okay, just tell them to wait.

79
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:06,889
-You know what to do.
-Yes, ma'am.

80
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:10,601
[suspenseful music playing]

81
00:05:27,535 --> 00:05:29,996
Mom, let's move, okay?

82
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:35,251
To a nicer room. Here, Mom.

83
00:05:38,087 --> 00:05:39,130
Mom…

84
00:05:42,383 --> 00:05:44,761
I'm sorry, but can you
please stay here awhile?

85
00:05:45,261 --> 00:05:46,763
I'll just attend to some guests.

86
00:05:47,138 --> 00:05:50,683
Um, please stay here. Don't go out, okay?

87
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:53,311
But we're not done reading yet.

88
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:55,688
I know, Mom. Here.

89
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:59,067
Feel free to read these while I'm away.

90
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:03,029
Don't worry. I'll be back soon.
This won't take long, okay?

91
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:05,114
Go on, read them.

92
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:07,283
Nurse.

93
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:11,204
Listen carefully.

94
00:06:12,413 --> 00:06:15,583
Do everything you can to make
my mother stay calm, okay?

95
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:18,711
Everything you need, including
reading materials, food,

96
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:21,714
and medicine, are all in there.
Don't let her go out.

97
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:23,091
Lock the door, okay?

98
00:06:23,674 --> 00:06:25,968
No one else must see her.

99
00:06:26,719 --> 00:06:29,347
Oh, my! What's taking her so long?

100
00:06:29,514 --> 00:06:30,807
We're going in now, okay?

101
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:32,100
Ma'am, wait…

102
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:34,227
We're going in. Can you
get out of my way, please?

103
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:36,145
-Excuse me.
-Ma'am, wait, ma'am.

104
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:37,355
Excuse me, ma'am.

105
00:06:37,438 --> 00:06:38,648
Now go back inside.

106
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:45,029
[suspenseful music playing]

107
00:06:45,571 --> 00:06:47,156
Ma'am, wait… Ma'am.

108
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:51,577
Thank you. Isn't she ready yet?

109
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:54,080
-Please wait here, ma'am.
-Yeah.

110
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:58,209
[suspenseful music playing]

111
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:12,515
Ma'am, they're waiting outside.

112
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:13,975
You know what to do.

113
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:16,519
They must not see my mother.

114
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:19,147
-There's no room for mistakes!
-Yes, ma'am.

115
00:07:28,239 --> 00:07:30,616
Ma'am, sir, Miss Aguas can see you now.

116
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:31,659
Wow! Finally.

117
00:07:31,742 --> 00:07:33,453
-This way, please.
-Arnaldo, let's go.

118
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:40,585
Thank you.

119
00:07:44,672 --> 00:07:45,673
Ivy!

120
00:07:59,061 --> 00:08:00,688
-Emilia!
-Long time no see!

121
00:08:00,771 --> 00:08:02,607
-Mr. Mayor.
-Miss Aguas.

122
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:04,525
What a pleasant surprise.

123
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:05,693
[smooches]

124
00:08:08,237 --> 00:08:10,531
You have a beautiful house.

125
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:13,451
No wonder you haven't
come back to Ardiente.

126
00:08:13,951 --> 00:08:16,078
Are you here to take me back?

127
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:20,374
Arnaldo, get us a bottle
of wine from the bar.

128
00:08:20,458 --> 00:08:22,418
Ivy and I have some business to discuss.

129
00:08:23,085 --> 00:08:24,504
-Okay.
-Thanks.

130
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:30,259
Actually, Ivy,
I need something else from you.

131
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:34,722
Well…

132
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:37,975
I need funding…

133
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:40,102
for my future endeavor.

134
00:08:41,395 --> 00:08:44,023
-Future endeavor?
-Yes.

135
00:08:44,732 --> 00:08:47,401
For my return as governor.

136
00:08:48,819 --> 00:08:50,321
You know what I mean.

137
00:08:52,406 --> 00:08:55,952
Emilia, I need a more convincing pitch.

138
00:08:56,202 --> 00:08:58,621
Well, I'll go straight to the point, Ivy.

139
00:08:58,829 --> 00:09:02,291
I need a huge sum of money
to get back into power

140
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:07,004
and stop my enemies' plans against me.

141
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:09,340
Like this one person.

142
00:09:09,423 --> 00:09:11,342
I don't know if you're familiar with her.

143
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:13,636
Camia Cruz?

144
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:16,514
[dramatic music playing]

145
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:34,907
-[Tonio] <i>Hey!</i>
-[Camia crying]

146
00:09:35,241 --> 00:09:39,036
<i>Lily… Run! Run!</i>

147
00:09:41,455 --> 00:09:42,498
Lily…

148
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:45,876
I got separated from her.
I told her to run.

149
00:09:50,047 --> 00:09:51,424
Camia Cruz?

150
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:56,971
Doesn't ring a bell.

151
00:09:58,306 --> 00:10:01,183
Besides, what's in it for me, Emilia?

152
00:10:02,101 --> 00:10:05,146
Why would I invest in something…

153
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:10,234
or someone who's bankrupt
and lost everything?

154
00:10:14,655 --> 00:10:20,578
Ivy, I may have fallen now.
But you know? I will rise again.

155
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:24,999
I don't want to leave you behind
while I'm on top.

156
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:26,334
[suspenseful sting]

157
00:10:26,417 --> 00:10:30,463
[laughs]

158
00:10:31,797 --> 00:10:32,965
Was that a joke?

159
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:34,258
[laughs]

160
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:38,346
Oh, I'm sorry, I thought it was a joke.

161
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:41,932
I'm… I'm so sorry for laughing, Emilia.

162
00:10:42,558 --> 00:10:43,559
[laughs]

163
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:45,853
Well, just so you know,

164
00:10:45,936 --> 00:10:48,606
I'm the only Ardiente
who'll work with you.

165
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:53,861
There is a witch-hunt ongoing,
and you're first on Papa's list.

166
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:56,656
It's okay. It's really fine.

167
00:10:56,864 --> 00:10:59,325
I'm not afraid of the congressman.

168
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:05,206
You know, Ivy, you may not
need me now, but soon, you will.

169
00:11:11,671 --> 00:11:15,216
[slow handclaps]

170
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:19,762
Bravo, Emilia. That was a good pitch.

171
00:11:20,846 --> 00:11:24,558
-Does that mean we have a deal?
-Of course, we have a deal.

172
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:26,685
[both chuckle]

173
00:11:38,823 --> 00:11:39,907
What do you want?

174
00:11:43,411 --> 00:11:47,206
Do you know just how
much trouble you've caused?

175
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:54,046
You and your women are the root
of this family's problems.

176
00:11:55,423 --> 00:12:00,344
And now, I have to find and bury someone…

177
00:12:01,554 --> 00:12:04,432
who should've died a long time ago.

178
00:12:05,599 --> 00:12:07,184
What are you talking about?
Get your hands off me!

179
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:09,353
We're just talking! What is this about?!

180
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:11,313
And your son, Diego?

181
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:15,818
He doesn't deserve
to carry the Ardiente name.

182
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:19,363
He's always ruining my plans.

183
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:23,868
But he should be thankful
I'm a good person.

184
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:28,038
If I weren't, I would've
told him the truth years ago.

185
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:30,332
What do you want to say to my son?

186
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:32,626
You know? Wait!

187
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:36,922
Whatever it is, I already told him.

188
00:12:37,006 --> 00:12:39,675
So, if you have something to
say, say it to me!

189
00:12:39,758 --> 00:12:42,136
I'm the father,
and you can't even face me!

190
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:44,722
-We'll see.
-Then get up!

191
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:45,806
Stop hiding behind your bodyguards.

192
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:46,849
-Hit him hard.
-Are you scared?

193
00:12:46,932 --> 00:12:47,933
[groans]

194
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:49,226
[Julio] Oh! Wait!

195
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:53,063
Beat him up, but don't touch his face.

196
00:12:53,731 --> 00:12:55,733
I don't want people to see him

197
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:58,944
and figure out he's been injured.

198
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:01,489
Just hit his body. Do it!

199
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:05,493
[grunts and groans]

200
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:10,206
[panting]

201
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:13,417
Look at what you've done to my floor.

202
00:13:14,376 --> 00:13:16,670
How dare you stain it
with your dirty blood!

203
00:13:18,255 --> 00:13:19,798
Why, what's the matter?

204
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:22,676
Hmm? You think you can
bring me down with this?

205
00:13:23,552 --> 00:13:24,970
Well, you're wrong.

206
00:13:26,555 --> 00:13:28,599
You can't knock me down.

207
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:31,060
And you know that.

208
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:33,562
That's why this is all you can do to me!

209
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:37,566
Right? You can't take me!
But you know what?

210
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:39,818
It'd be better if you just killed me,

211
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:42,863
Papa.

212
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:54,416
[tense music playing]

213
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:58,546
One bottle of wine…

214
00:14:01,715 --> 00:14:02,716
Ivy?

215
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:06,262
-She's outside, Miss Camia.
-I want to see Ivy.

216
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:07,846
I need to tell her something.

217
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:10,140
But Miss Ivy said we can't go outside.

218
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:11,892
Thank you.

219
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:14,979
-I'll take care of you here.
-No, I need to talk to her now.

220
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:17,356
Miss Camia. Miss Camia, she'll be here--

221
00:14:17,439 --> 00:14:19,817
Let go of me! I just want to talk to Ivy.

222
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:24,196
-Miss Camia…
-Ouch! Ouch. Stop it!

223
00:14:24,738 --> 00:14:26,198
-Let go of me!
-[loud thud]

224
00:14:26,490 --> 00:14:27,616
What's that sound?

225
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:29,994
<i>Mom?</i>

226
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:33,664
-Miss Camia…
-Let go…

227
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:34,915
Miss Ivy will come back.

228
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:36,834
-I just want to talk to Ivy.
-She'll come back for you.

229
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:39,545
[tense music playing]

230
00:14:48,178 --> 00:14:49,346
Why are there nurses?

231
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:51,015
Maybe one of the guests is sick.

232
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:53,309
Wait, a guest?

233
00:14:53,392 --> 00:14:54,935
Isn't this resort temporarily closed?

234
00:14:56,061 --> 00:14:58,147
I'm not sure, sir. Excuse me.

235
00:15:03,861 --> 00:15:04,945
Ivy, wait…

236
00:15:06,488 --> 00:15:07,615
Ivy will come back here.

237
00:15:07,698 --> 00:15:09,241
-I need to see her.
-I told you…

238
00:15:09,325 --> 00:15:12,494
-I want to talk to her.
-Miss Ivy will be here soon.

239
00:15:14,455 --> 00:15:15,539
Mr. Mayor.

240
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:17,666
Do you need anything?

241
00:15:19,251 --> 00:15:21,712
-What's a nurse doing here?
-Oh…

242
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:24,715
I've been feeling under
the weather these past few days,

243
00:15:24,798 --> 00:15:27,801
so I called for a nurse and a doctor.

244
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:31,805
Let's go?

245
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:35,476
But, you know, what's that noise?

246
00:15:36,435 --> 00:15:39,146
Oh, right. Can you
please wait for me outside?

247
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:43,400
I'll just check on it.
It might've been the wind.

248
00:15:43,484 --> 00:15:45,027
The breeze gets pretty strong here.

249
00:15:45,235 --> 00:15:48,530
-Oh, okay.
-Ria? Ria?

250
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:51,825
-Yes, ma'am?
-Did something fall?

251
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:53,410
Was it because of the wind again?

252
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:57,081
Oh yes, ma'am! It's very windy
outside so something fell again.

253
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:00,376
-Then fix it, please.
-Yes, ma'am.

254
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:04,672
I told you, it's really windy
in this resort.

255
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:06,715
-Let's go?
-Okay…

256
00:16:06,799 --> 00:16:09,218
[tense music playing]

257
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:14,848
Now, it's becoming clear to me.

258
00:16:17,267 --> 00:16:23,732
Miss Aguas gave this land to
the farmers to win their trust.

259
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:31,949
Miss Aguas is giving them the illusion…

260
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:37,955
that they have rights and power
over the land and their lives.

261
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:41,834
And I can't let them believe in that.

262
00:16:42,543 --> 00:16:48,382
Because worker ants don't have
the right to govern themselves.

263
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:51,635
I need to put them back in their place.

264
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:55,973
Like the slaves they are.

265
00:16:58,559 --> 00:17:00,644
So, what's your plan now, Congressman?

266
00:17:01,812 --> 00:17:05,983
I'll remind them I'm still
the ruler of this town.

267
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:10,863
And I will need your help, William.

268
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:26,420
Bye, Ivy. Thanks again.

269
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:29,548
-So, it's a deal?
-Yes, of course, Emilia.

270
00:17:30,799 --> 00:17:33,302
-Great! Thank you.
-Drive safe.

271
00:17:35,721 --> 00:17:38,474
<i>As long as you're indebted to me…</i>

272
00:17:38,974 --> 00:17:42,686
<i>you are now my slave, Emilia.</i>

273
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:49,818
We're really sorry, Governor Alvarez.

274
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:52,321
We really don't know where Miss Ivy is.

275
00:17:52,404 --> 00:17:54,740
And it's impossible for us to hide her.

276
00:17:54,948 --> 00:17:57,451
Yes, we know she bought us land,

277
00:17:57,534 --> 00:17:59,745
but we remain loyal to the Ardientes!

278
00:17:59,828 --> 00:18:01,914
[chuckles] You liars!

279
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:04,708
Go! Search the area!

280
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:07,294
-Hang on! Sir, wait!
-No, sir! No!

281
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:13,509
[people clamoring]

282
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:17,346
Why are you doing this to us?!
You can't do this to us!

283
00:18:18,388 --> 00:18:19,515
I am the governor!

284
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:22,184
And that's what you get for being a rebel!

285
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:26,105
-Don't hurt her!
-This isn't right!

286
00:18:26,563 --> 00:18:30,025
If you want to punish us,
do it the right way!

287
00:18:30,275 --> 00:18:32,152
-You've got some nerve! Fine!
-No, Governor!

288
00:18:32,277 --> 00:18:34,363
-Take her!
-Governor, stop! Please!

289
00:18:34,446 --> 00:18:36,907
Please stop! Don't hurt
my daughter! Take me, instead!

290
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:42,037
You're really annoying me. Take him too!

291
00:18:43,455 --> 00:18:45,332
-Wait!
-Listen carefully!

292
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:48,210
From now on, this cooperative is closed!

293
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:52,881
All your things and your produce
belong to us! Go!

294
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:54,550
Seize everything here!

295
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:57,511
-What about our livelihood?!
-You all need to learn a lesson!

296
00:18:57,594 --> 00:19:00,514
[people clamoring]

297
00:19:02,474 --> 00:19:03,433
Mom?

298
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:06,520
Mom?

299
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:09,523
Mom, I'm here.

300
00:19:09,606 --> 00:19:11,650
Why did you leave me, Ivy?

301
00:19:12,192 --> 00:19:16,905
Mom, I told you I had
some visitors, but I'm here now.

302
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:21,451
You left me. Why did you leave me?

303
00:19:25,122 --> 00:19:26,415
Mom, don't cry.

304
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:29,168
It's okay.

305
00:19:36,258 --> 00:19:39,303
-Dad!
-Let go of my daughter!

306
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:40,888
Let go of my daughter!

307
00:19:41,805 --> 00:19:44,099
Shut up! Do you want to suffer
like your dad?

308
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,685
Fernan! Fernan!

309
00:19:47,728 --> 00:19:48,729
[William] Take them!

310
00:19:49,104 --> 00:19:51,982
[people clamoring]

311
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:58,155
-Five, four, three…
-[people clamoring]

312
00:19:58,447 --> 00:19:59,990
Nimfa! Nimfa!

313
00:20:00,073 --> 00:20:01,742
…two, one.

314
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:03,911
-[William] Punish them! Go on!
-Now.

315
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,881
-Governor.
-Congressman.

316
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:24,681
I'm asking you to please stop
what you're doing for a second.

317
00:20:27,809 --> 00:20:28,936
Thank you.

318
00:20:34,983 --> 00:20:39,112
The people of Ardiente,
my beloved children.

319
00:20:40,447 --> 00:20:45,244
We here at Poblacion Ardiente
are like one huge family.

320
00:20:45,911 --> 00:20:49,289
A family that loves each other.

321
00:20:49,706 --> 00:20:52,960
But sometimes, when someone gets unruly…

322
00:20:53,418 --> 00:20:55,879
they need to be punished.

323
00:20:56,421 --> 00:20:59,341
Why is Governor Alvarez punishing you?

324
00:21:00,425 --> 00:21:04,221
This is not only for you
to hand over Ivy Aguas…

325
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:09,768
but for you to learn a lesson
for refusing to obey.

326
00:21:10,435 --> 00:21:14,147
You doubted the Ardiente
family's capability…

327
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:18,652
to properly govern this town.

328
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:24,866
The moment you got your own land,

329
00:21:25,242 --> 00:21:27,995
you thought you could live
by your own rules.

330
00:21:28,328 --> 00:21:32,291
Therefore, I'll make you feel…

331
00:21:32,916 --> 00:21:35,043
what it's like to own land

332
00:21:35,127 --> 00:21:37,129
without the government's support.

333
00:21:37,587 --> 00:21:40,590
From now on,
I'll close down the cooperative

334
00:21:40,716 --> 00:21:44,803
and cut the supply of water,
so you'll know…

335
00:21:45,178 --> 00:21:47,556
-No!
-how difficult it is to live

336
00:21:47,639 --> 00:21:50,350
without the government's support!

337
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:54,021
No, Señor Julio!
Where are you taking that?!

338
00:21:54,104 --> 00:21:59,776
[people clamoring]

339
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:05,449
Congressman, please forgive us.
We won't do it again.

340
00:22:06,074 --> 00:22:07,701
-Dad…
-We'll return the land.

341
00:22:09,494 --> 00:22:10,662
Fernan!

342
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:13,749
You know…

343
00:22:15,667 --> 00:22:17,794
this punishment is for your own good.

344
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:21,214
This is a lesson.

345
00:22:22,632 --> 00:22:27,596
Believe it or not,
it truly hurts me to do this.

346
00:22:29,097 --> 00:22:31,308
But, like a parent…

347
00:22:32,100 --> 00:22:34,811
if their children don't behave…

348
00:22:35,479 --> 00:22:39,483
they have to be disciplined,
even if it hurts.

349
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:43,820
One day, you'll thank me.

350
00:22:44,404 --> 00:22:48,325
This is proof of my love for you.

351
00:22:57,250 --> 00:22:58,668
-Dad! Dad!
-Nimfa!

352
00:22:59,586 --> 00:23:00,545
Dad.

353
00:23:00,629 --> 00:23:04,341
[tense music playing]

354
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:21,650
Did you see how I toyed
with the people of Ardiente?

355
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:28,532
How are you able to get them
to agree to whatever you say?

356
00:23:29,157 --> 00:23:32,744
I know how those peasants' minds work.

357
00:23:34,704 --> 00:23:36,498
So predictable.

358
00:23:37,791 --> 00:23:40,877
Ivy Aguas is mistaken.

359
00:23:41,419 --> 00:23:43,338
She is so wrong.

360
00:23:45,674 --> 00:23:47,968
These people cannot be empowered.

361
00:23:48,510 --> 00:23:52,180
Even if you give them
the title of the land…

362
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:57,686
they're still stupid, ignorant slaves…

363
00:23:58,270 --> 00:24:00,522
who cannot think for themselves.

364
00:24:01,398 --> 00:24:02,399
Ah…

365
00:24:02,899 --> 00:24:07,487
Oh, well. Our good deed
for the day is done.

366
00:24:08,822 --> 00:24:11,283
Let's have lunch. Your treat.

367
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:13,869
Let's go. Drive on.

368
00:24:18,957 --> 00:24:20,709
Where are we going to look for Miss Ivy?

369
00:24:21,459 --> 00:24:23,003
Poor Fernan.

370
00:24:23,336 --> 00:24:26,506
When will Julio Ardiente give us a break?

371
00:24:26,590 --> 00:24:28,091
This isn't right.

372
00:24:28,633 --> 00:24:30,802
He's not a father, he's a dictator.

373
00:24:33,763 --> 00:24:34,764
Diego?

374
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:40,937
[panting]

375
00:24:43,190 --> 00:24:44,733
I'm not a real Ardiente.

376
00:24:46,443 --> 00:24:49,946
Emilia isn't my real mother.

377
00:24:50,780 --> 00:24:53,783
-What?
-Diego. Diego, wait. Diego!

378
00:24:54,409 --> 00:24:55,785
Diego, listen to us!

379
00:24:57,787 --> 00:24:59,080
Listen to us.

380
00:24:59,748 --> 00:25:03,418
Remember, we're here for you.

381
00:25:03,501 --> 00:25:06,630
And we love you more than anyone else.

382
00:25:06,713 --> 00:25:08,673
[tense music playing]

383
00:25:13,261 --> 00:25:14,554
[Pandoy] Diego, where are you going?

384
00:25:19,643 --> 00:25:22,229
We've tried every treatment possible,

385
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:24,522
but you can see

386
00:25:24,606 --> 00:25:28,944
how Camia's brain function
continues to degenerate.

387
00:25:29,027 --> 00:25:32,030
Have you decided if she'll undergo ECT?

388
00:25:33,156 --> 00:25:35,825
While we may not be sure
she'll get better, at least

389
00:25:35,909 --> 00:25:39,329
we tried everything before
going to the US for treatment.

390
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:42,415
Then again, miracles can happen.

391
00:25:47,254 --> 00:25:49,881
Dad? Where's my mother?

392
00:25:52,259 --> 00:25:53,843
Dad, please, answer me.

393
00:25:53,927 --> 00:25:56,263
Where's my real mother? I want to see her.

394
00:25:58,765 --> 00:26:01,518
Diego, I'm sorry, but that won't happen.

395
00:26:03,061 --> 00:26:05,063
You can't see your mother.

396
00:26:06,690 --> 00:26:08,942
What do you mean? Dad…

397
00:26:09,526 --> 00:26:12,153
-Dad, please.
-Diego, I know this is hard.

398
00:26:12,237 --> 00:26:14,572
But there's nothing I can do.

399
00:26:14,656 --> 00:26:16,408
You can't see her because…

400
00:26:17,867 --> 00:26:19,577
your mother's gone.

401
00:26:21,663 --> 00:26:23,415
Emilia had her killed.

402
00:26:23,498 --> 00:26:24,624
[suspenseful sting]

403
00:26:33,341 --> 00:26:34,342
No.

404
00:26:40,223 --> 00:26:42,517
No. That can't be. My mom isn't dead.

405
00:26:43,226 --> 00:26:44,311
Son…

406
00:26:47,188 --> 00:26:48,481
She's been dead for years.

407
00:26:50,483 --> 00:26:52,193
Emilia had her killed.

408
00:26:53,153 --> 00:26:54,821
I'm sorry I wasn't able to do anything.

409
00:26:55,822 --> 00:26:57,657
I wasn't able to protect your mother.

410
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:01,036
It's my fault. I'm sorry.

411
00:27:02,579 --> 00:27:03,705
No. No, Dad.

412
00:27:09,627 --> 00:27:12,964
Don't blame yourself. It's not your fault.

413
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:18,678
If there's anyone who needs to pay…

414
00:27:19,471 --> 00:27:20,972
for everything that happened to us,

415
00:27:21,056 --> 00:27:24,142
to you, me, and your mother…

416
00:27:24,851 --> 00:27:27,937
it's Emilia and Julio.

417
00:27:29,230 --> 00:27:30,523
The Ardientes.

418
00:27:44,662 --> 00:27:47,123
Mom, I agreed to do the procedure.

419
00:27:55,131 --> 00:27:57,300
Just like what Dad said…

420
00:28:02,222 --> 00:28:03,807
Learn to fight.

421
00:28:07,685 --> 00:28:09,062
Learn to take risks.

422
00:28:13,191 --> 00:28:14,776
And learn to have faith.

423
00:28:19,322 --> 00:28:22,117
[Ivy] <i>I love you and Dad so much.</i>

424
00:28:25,620 --> 00:28:27,414
<i>And the love I feel for you…</i>

425
00:28:30,875 --> 00:28:32,669
<i>gives me strength…</i>

426
00:28:36,339 --> 00:28:37,799
<i>to keep fighting…</i>

427
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:43,972
<i>to keep believing.</i>

428
00:28:52,856 --> 00:28:54,858
<i>Mom, I believe you'll get better.</i>

429
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:00,989
<i>You'll recover.</i>

430
00:29:03,825 --> 00:29:05,160
<i>You'll get better…</i>

431
00:29:09,706 --> 00:29:13,752
<i>because we still have to win this fight.</i>

432
00:29:17,672 --> 00:29:23,511
-[heart beating]
-[machine beeping rhythmically]

433
00:29:33,897 --> 00:29:36,065
[Dante] <i>Once we settle</i>
<i>in Poblacion Ardiente…</i>

434
00:29:36,149 --> 00:29:39,235
<i>I'll build my own private law firm.</i>

435
00:29:39,319 --> 00:29:43,448
[Camia] <i>Me too, hon. I'll put up</i>
<i>a weekend daycare center.</i>

436
00:29:43,531 --> 00:29:46,117
-<i>Dante? Dante!</i>
-[Dante grunting]

437
00:29:46,367 --> 00:29:49,871
<i>-What happened…</i>
<i>-Lily… Run!</i>

438
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:51,539
[groans]

439
00:29:51,915 --> 00:29:54,876
<i>I thought you were dead,</i>
<i>but you're alive, Mom!</i>

440
00:29:54,959 --> 00:29:56,461
<i>It's me, Lily.</i>

441
00:29:56,920 --> 00:30:00,507
<i>-Lily?</i>
<i>-You're looking at her, Mom.</i>

442
00:30:00,799 --> 00:30:02,842
<i>It's been 13 years already.</i>

443
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:09,432
<i>I'm not a kid anymore.</i>
<i>I'm all grown up. See? I'm Lily.</i>

444
00:30:12,435 --> 00:30:15,396
[tense music playing]

445
00:30:27,450 --> 00:30:30,453
[solemn music playing]

446
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:48,555
Mom.

447
00:30:53,476 --> 00:30:55,311
How are you feeling?

448
00:31:02,652 --> 00:31:03,695
Ivy.

449
00:31:09,033 --> 00:31:10,493
[pants]

450
00:31:10,577 --> 00:31:11,536
Lily…

451
00:31:18,042 --> 00:31:19,043
Lily.

452
00:31:24,674 --> 00:31:25,717
My Lily.

453
00:31:33,683 --> 00:31:36,936
-Mom?
-Lily, is it?

454
00:31:43,151 --> 00:31:46,070
Lily. My daughter.

455
00:31:48,948 --> 00:31:51,451
-Mom?
-My Lily.

456
00:31:53,286 --> 00:31:55,663
-Mom.
-My Lily…

457
00:31:57,707 --> 00:32:01,794
-Mom…
-You're all grown up.

458
00:32:03,087 --> 00:32:04,631
What happened?

459
00:32:05,214 --> 00:32:06,716
Look at you.

460
00:32:08,927 --> 00:32:10,428
You're all grown up.

461
00:32:13,306 --> 00:32:15,642
Do you remember me now?

462
00:32:16,434 --> 00:32:17,477
Yes.

463
00:32:18,394 --> 00:32:20,480
Do you remember me now, Mom?

464
00:32:22,649 --> 00:32:24,025
My daughter…

465
00:32:25,985 --> 00:32:29,697
So much… So much has happened.

466
00:32:35,453 --> 00:32:37,288
I'll tell you everything.

467
00:32:39,832 --> 00:32:41,876
It's a long story, but…

468
00:32:46,589 --> 00:32:48,883
Can I hold you?

469
00:32:49,634 --> 00:32:51,970
-Yes.
-You remember me!

470
00:32:52,053 --> 00:32:56,599
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]

471
00:32:56,683 --> 00:32:57,684
Mom…

472
00:32:58,685 --> 00:33:00,561
Mom…

473
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:04,565
-I love you so much!
-I love you too.

474
00:33:04,649 --> 00:33:06,985
I love you so much, Mom.

475
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:09,487
[sobbing]

476
00:33:09,570 --> 00:33:12,323
You remember me now!

477
00:33:13,449 --> 00:33:14,450
Ivy.

478
00:33:15,535 --> 00:33:20,039
Nanny Carlotta! My mom remembers me again!

479
00:33:21,666 --> 00:33:25,128
This is the moment I've been waiting for.

480
00:33:25,253 --> 00:33:26,295
[sobs]

481
00:33:27,839 --> 00:33:28,798
She's alive!

482
00:33:30,008 --> 00:33:31,134
Mom.

483
00:33:33,636 --> 00:33:35,888
This is Nanny Carlotta.

484
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:38,141
All those years we were apart…

485
00:33:38,725 --> 00:33:41,436
Nanny Carlotta took care of me.

486
00:33:42,645 --> 00:33:43,855
[Camia] Thank you.

487
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:55,700
Doc… Doc, thank you!

488
00:33:55,783 --> 00:33:58,703
Thank you! Thank you! Thank you so much!

489
00:33:58,911 --> 00:34:02,165
I must admit, that in my
whole medical career,

490
00:34:02,248 --> 00:34:03,332
this is the first time

491
00:34:03,416 --> 00:34:05,585
I've witnessed someone respond this fast

492
00:34:05,668 --> 00:34:07,962
to the treatment and recovery.

493
00:34:09,338 --> 00:34:11,049
It's a miracle!

494
00:34:12,258 --> 00:34:13,926
Thank you very much, Doctor.

495
00:34:14,677 --> 00:34:17,096
You should thank your daughter, Ivy.

496
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:18,806
She never gave up.

497
00:34:21,100 --> 00:34:24,645
Doc, my mother will only
keep getting better, right?

498
00:34:24,937 --> 00:34:28,691
We will continue her medication
and therapy.

499
00:34:28,983 --> 00:34:31,736
And I believe that with your
continued love and support,

500
00:34:31,861 --> 00:34:34,238
there's a huge chance
for her full recovery.

501
00:34:38,868 --> 00:34:40,036
Thank you.

502
00:34:43,206 --> 00:34:44,540
Really, thank you.

503
00:34:46,626 --> 00:34:47,794
Mom.

504
00:34:54,926 --> 00:34:58,763
Mom. I love you.

505
00:34:58,846 --> 00:35:01,265
-I love you too, Lily.
-I love you, Mom.

506
00:35:01,349 --> 00:35:04,936
I love you very much.
You mean everything to me.

507
00:35:08,898 --> 00:35:09,816
Diego…

508
00:35:09,899 --> 00:35:11,275
-Diego, where are you going?
-Diego!

509
00:35:11,359 --> 00:35:12,902
-Nanny, please let go of me.
-Answer us, Diego!

510
00:35:12,985 --> 00:35:15,029
-Why won't you talk to us?
-What's your problem? Diego!

511
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:16,572
Answer your Nanny Loring, Diego!

512
00:35:16,656 --> 00:35:18,324
I have something to take care of!

513
00:35:18,407 --> 00:35:19,951
And what would that be?!

514
00:35:20,201 --> 00:35:22,203
Nanny, Uncle, for once…

515
00:35:22,286 --> 00:35:23,579
-can't you just leave me be?!
-Why--

516
00:35:23,663 --> 00:35:25,706
You won't leave until you
tell us what happened!

517
00:35:25,790 --> 00:35:26,582
Pandoy!

518
00:35:26,666 --> 00:35:29,252
You might get yourself in
danger! Do you understand?!

519
00:35:30,378 --> 00:35:31,754
-What's happening to you?!
-What's the problem?!

520
00:35:31,838 --> 00:35:32,755
They killed my mother!

521
00:35:33,297 --> 00:35:35,758
There, I said it! They killed my mom.

522
00:35:36,884 --> 00:35:39,428
Dad told me Emilia had my real mom killed.

523
00:35:40,638 --> 00:35:42,390
-I'll make them pay!
-Diego! Diego!

524
00:35:42,473 --> 00:35:43,766
Diego, you won't leave here

525
00:35:43,850 --> 00:35:45,601
until you calm down. Do you understand?

526
00:35:45,685 --> 00:35:47,562
-What should I do, then?!
-Diego!

527
00:35:47,687 --> 00:35:49,981
You'll only get
yourself hurt if you do that!

528
00:35:50,064 --> 00:35:52,358
So I should I just wait and do nothing?!

529
00:35:52,441 --> 00:35:54,652
-Diego…
-They killed my mom!

530
00:35:55,236 --> 00:35:56,571
She didn't do anything wrong!

531
00:35:57,196 --> 00:35:59,574
She just loved Dad. Where's the justice?

532
00:35:59,740 --> 00:36:02,702
Why do we let the Ardientes
treat us like this?!

533
00:36:02,910 --> 00:36:04,954
-Listen to me.
-When will we do something?!

534
00:36:05,037 --> 00:36:07,081
-Listen to me first.
-Pandoy! Pandoy!

535
00:36:07,248 --> 00:36:09,417
-They will kill you!
-Pandoy! Pandoy!

536
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:12,378
The Ardientes will kill you!
Don't you get it?

537
00:36:12,461 --> 00:36:13,880
The Ardientes will kill you…

538
00:36:13,963 --> 00:36:16,382
-Pandoy!
-if you go against them!

539
00:36:16,465 --> 00:36:17,466
Pandoy!

540
00:36:17,884 --> 00:36:19,093
[Loring cries]

541
00:36:19,177 --> 00:36:20,178
Diego…

542
00:36:20,261 --> 00:36:26,893
Diego. If you still respect me
as your second father…

543
00:36:27,685 --> 00:36:29,061
you'll listen to me.

544
00:36:29,937 --> 00:36:33,274
You won't pick a fight with the Ardientes!

545
00:36:33,900 --> 00:36:38,404
-I won't let them kill you too.
-Pandoy!

546
00:36:38,613 --> 00:36:42,825
Pandoy. Diego! Pandoy!

547
00:36:43,534 --> 00:36:44,744
Diego…

548
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:47,622
Diego…

549
00:36:49,916 --> 00:36:50,917
Diego…

550
00:36:51,167 --> 00:36:52,168
[yowls]

551
00:36:56,505 --> 00:36:59,884
[somber music playing]

552
00:37:17,610 --> 00:37:18,819
How are you, Mom?

553
00:37:21,322 --> 00:37:23,241
Lily, I remember everything now.

554
00:37:24,909 --> 00:37:26,661
The moment your dad died…

555
00:37:27,620 --> 00:37:29,580
the things they did to me…

556
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:34,377
until the day we got separated.

557
00:37:36,128 --> 00:37:37,463
I remember now.

558
00:37:38,589 --> 00:37:40,174
Like it happened yesterday.

559
00:37:45,221 --> 00:37:46,264
[exhales sharply]

560
00:37:47,723 --> 00:37:51,227
Lily, I know you're angry and hurt

561
00:37:51,978 --> 00:37:54,063
because I feel that way too.

562
00:37:55,564 --> 00:37:57,149
But I want to help you.

563
00:37:59,026 --> 00:38:01,570
I want to know what happened

564
00:38:01,654 --> 00:38:03,322
after your father and I lost you.

565
00:38:04,532 --> 00:38:06,617
How you became Ivy Aguas.

566
00:38:07,910 --> 00:38:09,412
It's all because of Miss Prianka.

567
00:38:11,163 --> 00:38:16,252
<i>She's how I became Ivy Aguas.</i>

568
00:38:16,961 --> 00:38:21,090
<i>She took me in. She helped and taught me…</i>

569
00:38:23,009 --> 00:38:25,261
to fight the Ardientes.

570
00:38:26,554 --> 00:38:30,391
If it weren't for Miss Prianka,
I'd probably be dead by now.

571
00:38:31,475 --> 00:38:33,644
Then I'm grateful to her.

572
00:38:35,646 --> 00:38:37,148
But as your mother…

573
00:38:37,732 --> 00:38:41,610
I should tell you not to seek vengeance.

574
00:38:43,696 --> 00:38:45,656
That you must learn to forgive.

575
00:38:46,073 --> 00:38:47,491
[exhales] But then…

576
00:38:48,909 --> 00:38:50,661
that'd make me a hypocrite.

577
00:38:52,496 --> 00:38:54,749
Because I can't forgive them, either.

578
00:38:56,542 --> 00:39:00,671
I understand why you'd want
revenge on the Ardientes.

579
00:39:01,213 --> 00:39:04,091
But I'm just worried about your safety.

580
00:39:06,552 --> 00:39:08,721
You have nothing to worry about.

581
00:39:09,805 --> 00:39:11,932
What's important is that we're safe.

582
00:39:12,016 --> 00:39:13,476
And I'll do everything…

583
00:39:15,144 --> 00:39:16,812
I'll do everything, Mom.

584
00:39:17,646 --> 00:39:20,024
Are you still planning to seek revenge?

585
00:39:22,902 --> 00:39:26,822
Mom… We'll talk about
that some other time.

586
00:39:27,698 --> 00:39:29,617
Get some rest for now.

587
00:39:29,909 --> 00:39:32,203
I want to visit your father's grave.

588
00:39:32,828 --> 00:39:34,497
I want to see him.

589
00:39:49,845 --> 00:39:51,263
Mom, for now…

590
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:56,769
this ring will have to do.

591
00:39:58,270 --> 00:40:02,316
Because I can't let you
go back to Poblacion Ardiente.

592
00:40:03,651 --> 00:40:06,070
If they find out you're alive,

593
00:40:06,487 --> 00:40:09,532
I'm sure they'll have you killed.

594
00:40:10,741 --> 00:40:12,660
I won't let that happen.

595
00:40:14,537 --> 00:40:18,624
I won't lose you all over again.

596
00:40:23,504 --> 00:40:26,340
What the Ardientes
are doing to us isn't right.

597
00:40:27,258 --> 00:40:30,928
They're walking all over us!
How do we get our land back?

598
00:40:31,554 --> 00:40:33,889
-What's going on here?
-Diego…

599
00:40:34,306 --> 00:40:36,976
Nimfa, Mr. Fernan, what happened?

600
00:40:37,226 --> 00:40:40,688
Governor Alvarez confiscated
our rice and money

601
00:40:40,980 --> 00:40:42,231
and closed down the cooperative.

602
00:40:42,314 --> 00:40:43,232
What?

603
00:40:43,315 --> 00:40:45,484
It's a good thing Señor Julio came.

604
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:48,112
If not, things could've been worse.

605
00:40:48,863 --> 00:40:51,449
The Congressman spoke to Governor.

606
00:40:51,782 --> 00:40:55,035
But they still have our money and crops.

607
00:40:55,119 --> 00:40:56,162
What was the point of it?

608
00:40:56,245 --> 00:40:58,747
I'm sure the Ardientes
have something to do with this.

609
00:40:59,081 --> 00:41:00,833
The congressman is a fraud.

610
00:41:00,916 --> 00:41:03,294
They'll do anything to get our land.

611
00:41:03,586 --> 00:41:05,671
How could you say that
about your own family?

612
00:41:06,505 --> 00:41:09,758
I'm not trying to ruin them.
I'm just telling the truth.

613
00:41:10,718 --> 00:41:12,970
The Ardientes were never on our side.

614
00:41:25,774 --> 00:41:30,738
I won't ever let anyone,

615
00:41:30,988 --> 00:41:35,701
especially the Ardientes,
hurt you and our family.

616
00:41:36,035 --> 00:41:37,244
No matter what.

617
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:42,958
[man] We all know they're
taking advantage of us.

618
00:41:43,167 --> 00:41:44,668
But can we do something about it?

619
00:41:44,919 --> 00:41:46,003
We can.

620
00:41:46,587 --> 00:41:48,923
But we don't need to resort to violence.

621
00:41:49,256 --> 00:41:52,092
We'll do this the right way. Legally.

622
00:41:52,301 --> 00:41:54,595
Legally? Is this legal?

623
00:41:54,803 --> 00:41:56,055
That's nonsense, Diego.

624
00:41:56,138 --> 00:41:58,307
We have to abide by the law.

625
00:41:58,390 --> 00:42:01,018
The Ardientes are the law in this place!

626
00:42:02,645 --> 00:42:03,938
They hurt my daughter.

627
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:06,857
Should I wait for them
to massacre my family

628
00:42:06,941 --> 00:42:08,150
before I make a move?

629
00:42:08,442 --> 00:42:12,571
It's only fair that
we should fight fire with fire.

630
00:42:13,239 --> 00:42:15,074
[all] He's right.

631
00:42:15,157 --> 00:42:16,784
Give them a taste of their own medicine.

632
00:42:16,992 --> 00:42:18,577
-They've gone too far.
-Fernan is right.

633
00:42:18,661 --> 00:42:20,079
We're being played.

634
00:42:20,955 --> 00:42:22,623
[Ivy] <i>I promise you, Mom.</i>

635
00:42:23,916 --> 00:42:27,503
The Ardientes will all burn in hell.

636
00:42:29,004 --> 00:42:31,674
I'll take away their power…

637
00:42:32,591 --> 00:42:36,971
until they crawl in the mud
where they belong.

638
00:42:38,597 --> 00:42:39,807
I swear it.

639
00:42:48,941 --> 00:42:50,651
-Nanny Carlotta.
-Ivy.

640
00:42:50,985 --> 00:42:54,572
-Ivy, come in.
-Where are the--

641
00:42:54,655 --> 00:42:56,532
Ivy, where's your mother?

642
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:59,285
She's in her room, resting.

643
00:43:00,369 --> 00:43:02,830
Ivy, I'm so happy for you.

644
00:43:03,330 --> 00:43:04,957
I know what you had to go through

645
00:43:05,040 --> 00:43:06,375
before finding your mother.

646
00:43:08,669 --> 00:43:10,129
Nanny, all I'm hoping for now

647
00:43:10,212 --> 00:43:11,797
is that we'll always be together.

648
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:16,385
I hope we can live a happy and quiet life.

649
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:21,348
Wait, you must be tired from the drive.

650
00:43:21,432 --> 00:43:22,641
-Have something to drink.
-Thank you.

651
00:43:22,725 --> 00:43:23,601
[phone rings]

652
00:43:25,894 --> 00:43:27,104
[phone ringing]

653
00:43:28,105 --> 00:43:29,231
It's Jepoy.

654
00:43:31,066 --> 00:43:31,984
Jepoy?

655
00:43:32,067 --> 00:43:33,527
Hello, Ivy.
Did the Governor track you down?

656
00:43:34,028 --> 00:43:35,696
Yes, Emilia found us.

657
00:43:35,904 --> 00:43:37,448
<i>But she doesn't know anything.</i>

658
00:43:37,531 --> 00:43:38,907
<i>She didn't see my mom.</i>

659
00:43:39,199 --> 00:43:42,286
And she should think twice
about ratting me out

660
00:43:42,453 --> 00:43:45,539
if she doesn't want me to reveal
her plans against her father.

661
00:43:45,706 --> 00:43:47,333
But you still need to be careful, Ivy.

662
00:43:47,416 --> 00:43:50,294
<i>The congressman's still</i>
<i>looking for you. He suspects…</i>

663
00:43:50,377 --> 00:43:52,379
that the farmers you helped
are protecting you.

664
00:43:53,756 --> 00:43:55,674
Wait. Do you know
what he did to the farmers?

665
00:43:56,342 --> 00:43:58,344
-No, why?
<i>-Ivy, you're not going to like</i>

666
00:43:58,427 --> 00:44:00,012
<i>what the congressman did to them.</i>

667
00:44:00,471 --> 00:44:02,139
He shut down the cooperative.

668
00:44:02,264 --> 00:44:04,183
<i>He confiscated all the farmers' money and…</i>

669
00:44:04,266 --> 00:44:05,934
produce to punish them.

670
00:44:11,690 --> 00:44:12,650
Diego…

671
00:44:13,025 --> 00:44:17,029
If you think Pandoy and I
will give you our blessing

672
00:44:17,112 --> 00:44:20,032
to fight the Ardientes, you're mistaken.

673
00:44:20,783 --> 00:44:23,744
I will accept any difficulty
that will come my way.

674
00:44:24,578 --> 00:44:28,165
I'll bow down before them if I have to…

675
00:44:29,667 --> 00:44:31,293
as long as they don't hurt you.

676
00:44:35,673 --> 00:44:37,758
Governor Alvarez is a puppet.

677
00:44:38,175 --> 00:44:43,055
I'm sure the congressman ordered
him to punish the farmers.

678
00:44:43,681 --> 00:44:46,892
Ivy, don't… Stay out of this.

679
00:44:47,184 --> 00:44:51,688
You're with your mother now.
Think about your safety.

680
00:44:54,900 --> 00:44:56,527
You're right, Nanny Carlotta.

681
00:44:57,152 --> 00:45:00,155
I need to prioritize my mother's safety.

682
00:45:01,115 --> 00:45:02,116
You're right.

683
00:45:05,160 --> 00:45:06,120
Here's what we'll do.

684
00:45:07,454 --> 00:45:09,373
You and Mom will go
to our house in Manila.

685
00:45:10,457 --> 00:45:12,167
We'll double our security there.

686
00:45:12,376 --> 00:45:15,170
What about you? Aren't you coming too?

687
00:45:15,379 --> 00:45:19,174
I'm not coming, my fight against
the Ardientes isn't over.

688
00:45:19,550 --> 00:45:21,009
I have to fulfill my promise

689
00:45:21,093 --> 00:45:23,095
to the people of Poblacion Ardiente.

690
00:45:23,637 --> 00:45:26,974
And I still have to seek justice
for my father's death.

691
00:45:27,224 --> 00:45:29,726
I don't make promises that I can't keep.

692
00:45:30,519 --> 00:45:34,231
Ivy… I'm only thinking about your safety.

693
00:45:35,357 --> 00:45:37,568
Don't put yourself in harm's way.

694
00:45:37,985 --> 00:45:40,904
Thank you for your concern,
Nanny Carlotta.

695
00:45:42,656 --> 00:45:46,577
But nothing's going to change.
My decision is final.

696
00:45:47,494 --> 00:45:50,664
So, tomorrow, you're going to Manila.

697
00:45:51,331 --> 00:45:53,417
-Ivy--
-Please look after my mother.

698
00:45:54,293 --> 00:45:55,919
Take care of her.

699
00:46:02,134 --> 00:46:03,135
[Ivy] Mom?

700
00:46:12,019 --> 00:46:15,772
Tomorrow, you and Nanny Carlotta
are going to Manila.

701
00:46:16,440 --> 00:46:18,400
You'll stay in my house?

702
00:46:18,692 --> 00:46:21,570
Our house in Manila.

703
00:46:22,613 --> 00:46:24,656
Do you want to teach again, Mom?

704
00:46:25,157 --> 00:46:27,826
There are a lot of schools near our house.

705
00:46:28,577 --> 00:46:29,661
What about you?

706
00:46:32,080 --> 00:46:33,290
Mom…

707
00:46:33,832 --> 00:46:35,626
I have to stay here

708
00:46:35,709 --> 00:46:38,170
because there's something
I need to settle.

709
00:46:39,129 --> 00:46:42,925
Here? Or in Ardiente?

710
00:46:44,801 --> 00:46:45,802
Mom.

711
00:46:47,888 --> 00:46:49,681
Don't worry about me.

712
00:46:50,641 --> 00:46:52,309
I can take care of myself.

713
00:46:53,143 --> 00:46:56,730
Once I'm done with what I need to do,

714
00:46:57,481 --> 00:47:01,026
I'll go to Manila too. I promise. Okay?

715
00:47:06,657 --> 00:47:09,034
-Pandoy!
-Loring?

716
00:47:09,117 --> 00:47:13,080
-What's wrong?
-Pandoy! It's Diego!

717
00:47:13,163 --> 00:47:16,208
-What about him?
-Diego left.

718
00:47:16,291 --> 00:47:18,627
He might've gone to the Ardientes!

719
00:47:18,710 --> 00:47:20,546
-What?!
-[phone chimes]

720
00:47:20,629 --> 00:47:21,463
Who's that?

721
00:47:25,092 --> 00:47:26,426
-It's Diego.
-What?

722
00:47:27,970 --> 00:47:29,179
[Diego] <i>Nanny, Uncle…</i>

723
00:47:29,763 --> 00:47:31,932
<i>please forgive me</i>
<i>for what I'm about to do.</i>

724
00:47:33,809 --> 00:47:36,603
<i>I will never have peace</i>
<i>until I confront the people</i>

725
00:47:36,687 --> 00:47:38,021
<i>who murdered my mother.</i>

726
00:47:39,064 --> 00:47:41,108
<i>In case I'm not able to return,</i>

727
00:47:41,191 --> 00:47:43,735
<i>let's just accept that it's my fate.</i>

728
00:47:43,819 --> 00:47:47,698
<i>Please leave Ardiente</i>
<i>and don't ever come back.</i>

729
00:47:47,781 --> 00:47:51,076
<i>Don't do anything that may</i>
<i>put your lives in danger.</i>

730
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:55,622
<i>And always remember that I love you both.</i>

731
00:47:55,706 --> 00:47:58,041
[sobs]

732
00:48:00,544 --> 00:48:03,380
<i>Thank you for taking care of me…</i>

733
00:48:04,881 --> 00:48:07,426
<i>and giving me a home and a family.</i>

734
00:48:09,261 --> 00:48:13,098
<i>Two things the Ardientes deprived me of.</i>

735
00:48:13,181 --> 00:48:17,561
[tense music playing]

736
00:48:21,857 --> 00:48:23,275
<i>Did you have my real mother killed?</i>

737
00:48:23,984 --> 00:48:25,360
<i>-Diego!</i>
<i>-What are you going to do?!</i>

738
00:48:25,444 --> 00:48:27,738
<i>This family raised you,</i>
<i>and this is how you repay us?!</i>

739
00:48:27,821 --> 00:48:28,864
<i>Papa!</i>

740
00:48:28,947 --> 00:48:29,781
<i>Now, drive!</i>

741
00:48:29,865 --> 00:48:33,910
<i>I'll make you feel just</i>
<i>how much you deserve to suffer.</i>

742
00:48:33,994 --> 00:48:37,122
<i>How could you let this</i>
<i>happen to your son?!</i>

743
00:48:37,205 --> 00:48:38,415
[Fernan] <i>They showed us violence,</i>

744
00:48:38,498 --> 00:48:39,958
<i>and violence is what we'll give them back.</i>

745
00:48:40,042 --> 00:48:41,168
[grunting]

746
00:48:41,251 --> 00:48:43,837
<i>If you're going to fight the Ardientes,</i>

747
00:48:43,920 --> 00:48:46,465
<i>then I won't let you go alone.</i>
<i>I'll fight with you.</i>

748
00:48:47,591 --> 00:48:49,509
<i>Attorney, what can you say</i>
<i>to the Ardientes?</i>

749
00:48:49,593 --> 00:48:50,927
[lawyer] <i>We're coming for all of you.</i>

750
00:48:51,011 --> 00:48:52,679
[Emilia] <i>Who's behind this?</i>

751
00:48:54,348 --> 00:48:57,184
[theme music playing]
